@inject ApiMetadata Api

@* AppShell's Overview, written by hand after the selection and form field Overviews: the parts and
   variants, each a page of its own in a frame with a phone width, then bar colors and the brand as
   code. Width and scrolling, and asides, are topics of their own (Docs/Topics/AppShell*Topic).
   Parts, Accessibility and See also come from the metadata and the doc comments; See also adds the demos. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor" Title="MainLayout.razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>An app shell is the frame around every page of an app: a header, a sidebar, the main area, and optionally an aside and a footer. Put it in your layout, around <Code>@@Body</Code>. The parts arrange themselves with CSS alone, so a static page arrives laid out and works <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">with JavaScript off</Anchor>.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>The shell starts with a "Skip to content" link to <Code>AppMain</Code>, whose id is <Code>ib-main</Code>. To change the id, set <Code>MainId</Code> on the shell.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Topics</Heading>
<OverviewTopics Component="Component" />

<Heading Level="2">Page regions</Heading>
<TextBlock>Each part of the shell is a region of the page: <Code>AppHeader</Code>, <Code>AppSidebar</Code>, <Code>AppMain</Code>, <Code>AppAside</Code> and <Code>AppFooter</Code>. Write the ones you need, in any order. Each part goes to its own place, and a part you leave out leaves no gap.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="app-shell-parts" WidthSwitch />
<TextBlock>At phone width the sidebar becomes a drawer behind the menu button (<Code>SidebarToggle</Code>), and the aside hides. Each changes below its own <Code>Breakpoint</Code>; this example sets 768px for both. The <Anchor Href="docs/components/app-sidebar">AppSidebar</Anchor> page covers the drawer, an icon rail and a panel under the header.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Variants</Heading>
<TextBlock>A variant sets how the parts are layered. Set <Code>Variant</Code> to choose one:</TextBlock>
<Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Variant</th><th>Look</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><Code>Tinted</Code> (default)</td><td>The sidebar is tinted.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>Inset</Code></td><td>The main area is raised as a panel in a tinted frame.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>Flat</Code></td><td>One surface, with lines between the parts.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>Canvas</Code></td><td>The main area is tinted, so cards stand out.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</Prose>
<ExampleViewer Example="app-shell-variants" WidthSwitch />
<TextBlock>Put a <Code>Canvas</Code> page's content in <Anchor Href="docs/components/card">Cards</Anchor>. Fills placed straight on the tint look like holes. To remove the lines between the parts when their colors already tell them apart, set <Code>Dividers="false"</Code>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Bars and colors</Heading>
<TextBlock>Each part can have its own background or color scheme, such as a dark sidebar in a light app. Set <Code>Bg</Code> or <Code>ColorScheme</Code> on the part. To set whether the header or footer stays in view as the page scrolls, set <Code>Position</Code> on <Code>AppHeader</Code> or <Code>AppFooter</Code>. The header stays in view by default; the footer doesn't.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Bars</Code>
<TextBlock>Text on a <Code>Bg</Code> uses the color's matching text color when it has one. Everything inside a part with a <Code>ColorScheme</Code> follows that scheme, its menus included. The <Anchor Href="demos/app-sidebar/full-height">full-height sidebar demo</Anchor> has a dark sidebar in a light app.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">The brand</Heading>
<TextBlock>The brand is the app's name in the header, with an icon or logo before it. Add an <Code>AppBrand</Code> and set <Code>Icon</Code> or <Code>Logo</Code>. To link it home, set <Code>Href</Code>. To show only a logo that already spells the name, set <Code>HideLabel</Code>.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Brand</Code>
<TextBlock>The name stays on one line. On a narrow screen it's cut short with an ellipsis rather than pushing the header's buttons off. A sidebar with no <Code>SidebarHeader</Code> shows the brand in its drawer's top row too.</TextBlock>

@if (OverviewParts.Of(Component, Api).Count > 0)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Parts</Heading>
}
<OverviewParts Component="Component" />

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        @inherits LayoutComponentBase

        <AppShell>
            <AppHeader>
                <SidebarToggle />
                <AppBrand Href="/" Icon="Lucide.Zap" Label="Acme" />
            </AppHeader>
            <AppSidebar>
                <NavMenu>
                    <NavItem Href="/" Icon="Lucide.House">Home</NavItem>
                    <NavItem Href="/projects" Icon="Lucide.Folder">Projects</NavItem>
                </NavMenu>
            </AppSidebar>
            <AppMain>@Body</AppMain>
        </AppShell>
        """;

    private const string Bars = """
        <AppShell>
            <AppHeader Bg="Color.FillSubtle">...</AppHeader>
            <AppSidebar ColorScheme="ColorScheme.Dark">...</AppSidebar>
            <AppMain>@Body</AppMain>
            <AppFooter Position="BarPosition.Sticky">...</AppFooter>
        </AppShell>
        """;

    private const string Brand = """
        <AppHeader>
            <SidebarToggle />
            <AppBrand Href="/" Label="Acme" HideLabel>
                <Logo><img src="logo.svg" alt="" width="96" height="24" /></Logo>
            </AppBrand>
        </AppHeader>
        """;
}
